# Wave W17-X (Route 209): pilgrim post — a pilgrim marker post where the flower drifts bank the fence: a weathered post carrying a flat stone cap and one small pale bell-mark band, the tower’s bell kept at pocket scale (design: the Forsaken Tower standing in its fenced plot with its bell in the belfry arch; the drifts bank at its fence). On tower turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from the fleet’s banded posts by the cap and the bell-mark: mileposts measure, relic posts warn of rings, this post only remembers.
